From: DE25-Nano port
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reassert Menu sixteen-row OSD

Older OSD implementations clear their high-resolution latch on each disable
transaction. Main can later enable a partially updated Menu screen without
writing line 8, leaving only the upper eight rows visible. Select the Menu
bitmap geometry immediately before every enable transaction.

diff --git a/osd.cpp b/osd.cpp
--- a/osd.cpp
+++ b/osd.cpp
@@ -502,6 +502,10 @@ void OsdEnable(unsigned char mode)
 {
 	user_io_osd_key_enable(mode & DISABLE_KEYBOARD);
 	mode &= (DISABLE_KEYBOARD | OSD_MSG);
+	// Explicitly reassert Menu's high-resolution (16-row) geometry before each
+	// enable. This also keeps Main compatible with older OSD implementations
+	// that clear the geometry latch on disable.
+	if (is_menu()) spi_osd_cmd(OSD_CMD_WRITE | 8);
 	spi_osd_cmd(OSD_CMD_ENABLE | mode);
 }
 
